    <item>
      <title>Solved: How to Fix &#39;unbound method f must be called with fibo instance as first argument got classobj instance instead&#39; Error in Python</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/python/solved-how-to-fix-unbound-method-error-in-python/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 05 Dec 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/python/solved-how-to-fix-unbound-method-error-in-python/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;question&#34;&gt;Question:&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;While working with classes in Python, I encountered a frustrating error when attempting to call a method on my class instance. The specific error message displayed was as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Traceback (most recent call last):&#xA; File &amp;#34;C:\Users\domenico\Desktop\py\main.py&amp;#34;, line 8, in &amp;lt;module&amp;gt;&#xA; fibo.f()&#xA; TypeError: unbound method f() must be called with fibo instance as first argument (got nothing instead)&#xA;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s the relevant code snippet from my &lt;code&gt;swineflu.py&lt;/code&gt; file:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-python&#34; data-lang=&#34;python&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;fibo&lt;/span&gt;:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    a &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    b &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;(self, a&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;):&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        print(fibo&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;b &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; a)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        fibo&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;b &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; a&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; self(a &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;And in my &lt;code&gt;main.py&lt;/code&gt; script, I have:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Solved: Why do I get AttributeError &#39;NoneType&#39; object has no attribute &#39;something&#39;?</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/python/solved-why-do-i-get-attributerror-nonetype-object-has-no-attribute-something/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 05 Dec 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/python/solved-why-do-i-get-attributerror-nonetype-object-has-no-attribute-something/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I am encountering the error message:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-plaintext&#34; data-lang=&#34;plaintext&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;AttributeError: &amp;#39;NoneType&amp;#39; object has no attribute &amp;#39;something&amp;#39;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This post aims to unravel the intricacies of this particular error, highlighting significant causes of &lt;code&gt;AttributeError&lt;/code&gt; due to &lt;code&gt;NoneType&lt;/code&gt; objects and providing methods for troubleshooting.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;what-causes-this-error&#34;&gt;What Causes This Error?&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The error signifies that a variable you are trying to use is set to &lt;code&gt;None&lt;/code&gt;, and you’re attempting to access an attribute or method on that variable. There are several scenarios that might lead to encountering this error. Let’s explore some common ones.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
